Look up Active DNS observations for a domain name or an IP address.                       
                                                                                          
For a domain name, shows the records the name resolved to (A, AAAA, MX, NS, SOA, TXT). For
an IP address, shows the domain names that resolved to it.                                
                                                                                          
Several names or IPs can be given, up to 100: as positional arguments, comma-separated    
lists, or read from a file (or STDIN) with --input-file. Each input is looked up          
independently: if one fails, the rest still proceed.                                      
                                                                                          
Results cover a time window (default: the last 7 days). Use --timeline to show each       
observed time range instead of one row per record.                                        
                                                                                          
For the DNS names in a host's current record, use "censys view <ip>".                     
                                                                                          
This command is only available to organizations on the Censys Search and Censys Core      
plans.                                                                                    

Usage:
  censys dns <name|ip>... [flags]

Examples:
  censys dns censys.com
  censys dns censys.com --record-type A,MX
  censys dns censys.com --timeline --duration 90d
  censys dns 104.18.10.84
  censys dns 104.18.10.84 --start 2026-06-01T00:00:00Z --duration 30d
  censys dns 141.193.213.10 --timeline --domain censys.com
  censys dns censys.com,104.18.10.84
  censys dns --input-file iocs.txt
  censys dns --input-file - # read inputs from STDIN
  censys dns censys.com --output-format json

Flags:
      --domain string         limit an IP timeline to one domain name (IP input with --timeline only)
  -d, --duration string       time window (e.g., 1d, 1w, 1y, 2h). Defaults to 7d (default "168h0m0s")
  -e, --end string            end time
  -h, --help                  help for dns
  -i, --input-file string     file to read the names or IPs from (or - for STDIN). Overrides positional arguments.
  -p, --max-pages int         maximum number of pages to fetch (-1 for all pages) (default 10)
  -o, --org-id string         organization ID to target (personal access tokens only)
  -n, --page-size int         number of records to return per page (default 100)
  -r, --record-type strings   record types to include (A, AAAA, MX, NS, SOA, TXT; IP addresses support A and AAAA)
  -s, --start string          start time
  -t, --timeline              show one row per observed time range instead of one row per record

Global Flags:
      --debug                   enable debug logging
      --no-color                disable ANSI colors and styles
      --no-spinner              disable spinner during operations
  -O, --output-format string    output format (json|yaml|tree|short|template) (default "short")
  -q, --quiet                   suppress non-essential output
  -S, --streaming               enable streaming output mode (NDJSON) for commands that support it
      --timeout-http duration   per-request timeout for HTTP requests (e.g. 10s, 1m) - use 0 to disable

